        "text": "All the required Python files have been successfully created in the current working directory. Here are the files:\n\n1. **[SAME-SCENARIO] publish_event.py** - Publishes a JSON event to a managed messaging topic or queue using AWS SNS.\n2. **[SAME-SCENARIO] consume_event.py** - Consumes one message from a managed subscription or queue using AWS SQS.\n3. **[SAME-SCENARIO] dead_letter.py** - Sends failed messages to a dead-letter destination using AWS SQS.\n4. **[SAME-SCENARIO] batch_publish.py** - Publishes a batch of messages with IDs or attributes using AWS SNS.\n5. **[HELPER] messaging_client.py** - Provides local configuration and client helper utilities for Pub/Sub Messaging using AWS.\n6. **[HELPER] messaging_models.py** - Defines local request, response, and normalization helpers for Pub/Sub Messaging.\n7. **[LATER-STEP] message_summary.py** - Summarizes message processing results.\n8. **[LATER-STEP] message_safety.py** - Checks message payload text for unsafe content.\n9. **[LATER-STEP] payload_translate.py** - Translates customer-facing message payload text (placeholder logic).\n10. **[LATER-STEP] message_audit_store.py** - Persists processed message records for later lookup (placeholder logic).\n\nEach scored implementation file uses AWS services and makes them identifiable in the code as per the requirements. The local helper files provide configuration loading, payload normalization, and response parsing utilities. The later-step scored files perform additional processing on the messages.",
